"A subject of Wu-huai? A subject of Ko-t'ien?": "b70ac866b9f7",
"Beside his house stood five willow trees, and from these he took his name.": "36bc6691d8f1",
"By nature he loved wine, but his household was poor and he could not always have it. Relatives and old friends, knowing this, would sometimes set out wine and invite him over.": "34576f38fe7a",
"Deep in his cups he made poems, taking pleasure in his own mind.": "c2f6bf7078f7",
"He liked to read but did not press for exact explanations; whenever something struck him he would forget his meals for joy.": "f6e2e527b293",
"He often wrote pieces to amuse himself, and in them showed something of his mind. He put gain and loss out of thought, and so lived out his life.": "80cb2852333e",
"He was quiet and said little; he had no longing for glory or gain.": "d93369a8a3ed",
"In appraisal: the wife of Ch'ien Lou once said, He did not grieve over poverty and low station, nor was he anxious after wealth and rank.": "3c0a91a61717",
"No one knows where the gentleman came from, nor is his name or style recorded.": "8457f99cbfda",
"Push her words to their limit — is this not a man of that sort?": "cc681ceae7d6",
"The walls around him were bare and kept out neither wind nor sun; his short coarse coat was patched, his bowl and gourd were often empty — and he was at ease.": "f3538272c747",
"When he came he drank the cup dry; his aim was always to get drunk; and once drunk he withdrew, never making any fuss about staying or going.": "b4304472419d"
